        "title": "feat(ui): show agent avatars in the agents page selector",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Agents page agent picker was a native `<select>`, which renders OS chrome that ignores the app theme and cannot display agent identity avatars (image or emoji). With several agents configured, the switcher was a plain text list, inconsistent with the identity-aware chat and sessions surfaces.\n\nRefs #57067 (dropdown-friction issue; that broader \"visible list\" request stays open — this upgrades the dropdown itself).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAgent identities (avatar image, emoji, name) are already loaded on the Agents page (`ensureAgentIdentities`), but the native `<option>` element cannot render them. A custom HTML listbox is the standard way to get themed, image-capable options while keeping accessibility.\n\n- New light-DOM Lit component `openclaw-agent-select` (`ui/src/components/agent-select.ts`), following the `session-menu` interaction pattern: trigger button with `aria-haspopup=\"listbox\"`/`aria-expanded`, popup `role=\"listbox\"` with `role=\"option\"` buttons, arrow/Home/End roving focus (options are `tabindex=\"-1\"`), buffered printable-key type-ahead matching native `<select>` search, Escape/Tab/outside-pointerdown close, focus returned to the trigger. The trigger's accessible name is the selected agent's visible label, mirroring how the native select exposed its value.\n- Avatar resolution per agent: image URL (`resolveAgentAvatarUrl`) → identity emoji (`resolveAgentTextAvatar`, now exported) → uppercase initial. Local `/avatar/<agentId>` URLs need an Authorization header when gateway token auth is active and a bare `<img>` cannot send one, so the component fetches them with the bearer credential and renders cached `blob:` URLs (revoked on disconnect) — the same contract as `chat-avatar.ts`, with a text-avatar fallback while loading or on failure. The page passes `authToken` via `resolveControlUiAuthToken`.\n- Same behavior contract as the old select: `onSelectAgent` fires only on actual change, \"default\" badge, disabled-while-loading, \"No agents\" empty state.\n- Old `.agents-select` CSS replaced by `.agent-select__*` styles using the shared menu tokens (`--bg-elevated`, `--radius-lg`, session-menu shadow).\n\nSibling surface note: the Dreams page keeps its compact native `<select>` — it is a label-only filter without identity data loaded; converting it is a separate follow-up if wanted.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe Agents page selector now shows each agent's avatar/emoji/initial next to its name in a themed dropdown (light + dark), with a \"default\" badge and check mark on the selected agent. Keyboard and screen-reader semantics move from native select to listbox pattern.\n\nClosed:\n\n![closed dark](https://github.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/releases/download/agent-select-avatars/agent-select-closed-dark.png)\n\nOpen (dark / light):\n\n![open dark](https://github.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/releases/download/agent-select-avatars/agent-select-open-crop-dark.png)\n![open light](https://github.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/releases/download/agent-select-avatars/agent-select-open-crop-light.png)\n\n(Shots from the mock-gateway Playwright harness: image avatar on `main`, emoji on `blockdigest`, initial fallback on `clawblocker`.)\n\n## Evidence\n\n- New jsdom component tests (`ui/src/components/agent-select.test.ts`, 11 tests): image/data-URL avatar, emoji fallback, initial fallback, token-auth local-avatar blob-fetch contract (Authorization header, blob render, revoke on disconnect), listbox open/selection state, keyboard navigation incl. Tab-refocus and type-ahead, select/no-op-select, Escape/outside close, empty state.\n- `ui/src/pages/agents/view.test.ts`: renders the component with the agents list and selected label.\n- `ui/src/e2e/agents-set-default-persistence.e2e.test.ts` updated to drive the custom dropdown (trigger click + `role=option` click).\n- Focused runs: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/components/agent-select.test.ts ui/src/pages/agents/view.test.ts` → 20 passed.\n- Testbox `pnpm check:changed` (lint, tsgo typecheck lanes, guards) → exit 0.\n- Codex autoreview iterated to clean: accepted findings (Tab focus drop, trigger accessible name, missing type-ahead, authenticated local avatars) fixed with regression tests.\n",
